  abstract={This study utilizes ecocritical tenets to uncover oppressive eco-dramas out of waste, refuse, and obscurity. With littered landscapes and blurred boundaries between nonhuman and human existence as impetus, these poems unpack and explore the ecological dialectic to navigate the nonhuman perspective and decenter the human. Such tenets include the nexus between human culture and the physical world, the interconnectedness found in the life cycle of abiotic things, and the enlivened world of nonhuman animals.},
